{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21879388",
      "title": "Introducing Navigation Guards",
      "lectureOrder": 185,
      "videoOrder": 161,
      "sourceHash": "2a3a02f7a3e4129b49600a88a7f7eb7f1e9edad75bbd2ea171f4910a64ad686d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.14,
          "end": 3.48,
          "en": "The last feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.48,
          "end": 5.73,
          "en": "I wanna explore in this module with you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.73,
          "end": 8.41,
          "en": "is the feature of navigation guards.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.41,
          "end": 12.03,
          "en": "Navigation guards can be useful if you add features like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.03,
          "end": 14.89,
          "en": "authentication where you, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.89,
          "end": 18.45,
          "en": "want to avoid that a user is able to access a certain route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.45,
          "end": 20.69,
          "en": "if he or she is not authenticated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.69,
          "end": 22.08,
          "en": "but they can also be useful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.08,
          "end": 25.34,
          "en": "to simply be aware of changing pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.34,
          "end": 27.25,
          "en": "in case you wanna run some code there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.25,
          "end": 30.31,
          "en": "or they can be useful to ensure that a user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.31,
          "end": 33.24,
          "en": "doesn't accidentally navigate away from a page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.24,
          "end": 38.24,
          "en": "where he or she has unsaved edits in a forum, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.64,
          "end": 41.2,
          "en": "We'll see practical examples for guards",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.2,
          "end": 43.04,
          "en": "in the course project, but of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.04,
          "end": 45.94,
          "en": "since this is the introductory module to routing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.94,
          "end": 48.26,
          "en": "I'll start showing you all those guards",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.26,
          "end": 50.063,
          "en": "in this module already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.18,
          "end": 53.94,
          "en": "Now, what exactly do I mean, when I say guards?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.94,
          "end": 57.15,
          "en": "I'm talking about functions, methods,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.15,
          "end": 60.42,
          "en": "which are called automatically by view router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.42,
          "end": 63.98,
          "en": "when a page changes or to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.98,
          "end": 66.653,
          "en": "when a navigation action started.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.87,
          "end": 72.12,
          "en": "For example, on the router we're creating in main JS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.12,
          "end": 76.86,
          "en": "on this main router before we pass it to our view app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.86,
          "end": 81.41,
          "en": "we can call before each, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.41,
          "end": 83.51,
          "en": "Before each is a build in method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.51,
          "end": 88.11,
          "en": "and it wants a function as an argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.11,
          "end": 91.35,
          "en": "Before each once a function as an argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.35,
          "end": 94.75999999999999,
          "en": "And this function will be called by the view router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.75999999999999,
          "end": 98.52000000000001,
          "en": "whenever we navigate from one page to another.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.52000000000001,
          "end": 103.173,
          "en": "Before each navigation action, this function will be called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.47,
          "end": 106.3,
          "en": "And this function will then receive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.3,
          "end": 108.92,
          "en": "free arguments from your router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.92,
          "end": 112.83,
          "en": "to, which is the route object off the page we're going to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.83,
          "end": 115.31,
          "en": "from, which is the route object of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.31,
          "end": 117.03,
          "en": "the page where coming from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.03,
          "end": 121.27,
          "en": "and next, which is a function which we have to call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.27,
          "end": 126.27,
          "en": "to either confirm or cancel this navigation action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.3,
          "end": 130.33,
          "en": "Because that's something we can do in navigation guards",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.33,
          "end": 132.51,
          "en": "which is why they are called guards.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.51,
          "end": 136.59,
          "en": "We can cancel a navigation if we're not happy with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.59,
          "end": 140.32,
          "en": "If we, for example, want to deny the navigation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.32,
          "end": 142.743,
          "en": "because the user is not authenticated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.1,
          "end": 146.62,
          "en": "Now, how could this look like?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.62,
          "end": 150.77,
          "en": "First of all, I'm going to console log, to and from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.77,
          "end": 152.49,
          "en": "so that we see what we're getting there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.49,
          "end": 157.27,
          "en": "And then I'll call next like this, with no special setting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 157.27,
          "end": 161.03,
          "en": "I will also console log global",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 161.03,
          "end": 163.85,
          "en": "beforeEach to make it clear that we're in this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 163.85,
          "end": 168.463,
          "en": "globally on the entire router registered before each hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 169.93,
          "end": 174.04,
          "en": "If I saved that, reload and cleared a console",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.04,
          "end": 179.04,
          "en": "and I go to users, we see global before each in the console",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 179.05,
          "end": 181.243,
          "en": "and then we see two logs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 182.09,
          "end": 185.17,
          "en": "Now, one of these logs is coming from the scroll behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 185.17,
          "end": 188.26,
          "en": "So to avoid confusion, I'll comment this out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.26,
          "end": 190.54,
          "en": "and to avoid that my IDE complaints",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 190.54,
          "end": 193.5,
          "en": "about the unused to and from,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.5,
          "end": 197.79,
          "en": "I'll replace it with an underscore and underscore two,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 197.79,
          "end": 199.52,
          "en": "which is basically an indicator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 199.52,
          "end": 201.82999999999998,
          "en": "that I have to take these arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 201.82999999999998,
          "end": 203.69,
          "en": "in order to reach the third one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 203.69,
          "end": 205.633,
          "en": "but then I don't plan on using them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 206.56,
          "end": 210.28,
          "en": "That's something my IDE and my local setup will accept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 210.28,
          "end": 213.81,
          "en": "So these are just argument names, following a convention",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 213.81,
          "end": 215.92000000000002,
          "en": "that signals to the set up that I",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 215.92000000000002,
          "end": 219.023,
          "en": "need to use these arguments, but I don't plan on using them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 220.13,
          "end": 221.82999999999998,
          "en": "So with that, if I reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 221.82999999999998,
          "end": 223.92000000000002,
          "en": "and we switched from users to teams now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 223.92000000000002,
          "end": 226.69,
          "en": "we see global beforeEach and then one log",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 226.69,
          "end": 230.28,
          "en": "with the to and the from route object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 230.28,
          "end": 232.82999999999998,
          "en": "To, of course is having the team's path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 232.82999999999998,
          "end": 234.99,
          "en": "because we're going to teams",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 234.99,
          "end": 237.42000000000002,
          "en": "and from has users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 237.42000000000002,
          "end": 240.16,
          "en": "And other than that we see nothing special",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 240.16,
          "end": 242.73,
          "en": "because I just called next like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 242.73,
          "end": 244.66,
          "en": "And if you call next like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 244.66,
          "end": 248.003,
          "en": "you allow the navigation, you confirm it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 249.29,
          "end": 252.35,
          "en": "You can also pass false to next though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 252.35,
          "end": 255.66,
          "en": "And that will cancel the navigation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 255.66,
          "end": 256.92,
          "en": "Let's try that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 256.92,
          "end": 260.39,
          "en": "If I saved that, we already see when I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 260.39,
          "end": 262.19,
          "en": "there's nothing on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 262.19,
          "end": 263.87,
          "en": "because loading the page failed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 263.87,
          "end": 267.28,
          "en": "because I canceled this initial navigation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 267.28,
          "end": 270.95,
          "en": "If I try to go to users, we get no error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 270.95,
          "end": 274.97,
          "en": "We see our global before each method runs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 274.97,
          "end": 277.78,
          "en": "but again, we see nothing on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 277.78,
          "end": 280.773,
          "en": "because with false, we cancel this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 282.2,
          "end": 284.05,
          "en": "Now here, of course that's not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 284.05,
          "end": 287.69,
          "en": "too useful because we're canceling all navigation here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 287.69,
          "end": 289.7,
          "en": "but later in the course project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 289.7,
          "end": 294.19,
          "en": "we'll also see how we could use that feature in combination",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 294.19,
          "end": 298.33,
          "en": "with checking whether the user is authenticated or not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 298.33,
          "end": 301.14,
          "en": "to cancel or allow this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 301.14,
          "end": 305.53,
          "en": "We also have a third option for next here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 305.53,
          "end": 309.77,
          "en": "Besides passing nothing or false, we can also pass",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 309.77,
          "end": 313.43,
          "en": "either a string or a location object in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 313.43,
          "end": 317.46,
          "en": "A string with a route you wanna navigate to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 317.46,
          "end": 318.8,
          "en": "which of course should then be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 318.8,
          "end": 321.81,
          "en": "one of the routes we registered up there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 321.81,
          "end": 325.49,
          "en": "or such a navigation object which describes that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 325.49,
          "end": 327.4,
          "en": "For example, by using the name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 327.4,
          "end": 330.29,
          "en": "and then maybe setting up any parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 330.29,
          "end": 334.46,
          "en": "Like here, I could make sure that every navigation action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 334.46,
          "end": 337.9,
          "en": "leads to a route with the name team-members",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 337.9,
          "end": 341.49,
          "en": "and teamId set to t2,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 341.49,
          "end": 343.65,
          "en": "which of course makes absolutely no sense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 343.65,
          "end": 346.55,
          "en": "but I just want to show you how that works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 346.55,
          "end": 350.42,
          "en": "However, make sure you don't save and reload here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 350.42,
          "end": 352.44,
          "en": "because you would create an infinite loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 352.44,
          "end": 355.29,
          "en": "Because even when we go to this route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 355.29,
          "end": 359.94,
          "en": "because we redirect here, we would then again redirect us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 359.94,
          "end": 364.94,
          "en": "So here we should then actually check if to.path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 365.06,
          "end": 369.2,
          "en": "or to.name is equal to team members.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 369.2,
          "end": 372.25,
          "en": "So if we are already going to the team-members page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 372.25,
          "end": 374.33,
          "en": "in which case I wanna call next",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 374.33,
          "end": 377.24,
          "en": "and only else, if we're going to a different page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 377.24,
          "end": 380.403,
          "en": "I wanna forward, I wanna redirect to team-members.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 381.91,
          "end": 385.51,
          "en": "And now we can save this and reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 385.51,
          "end": 389.2,
          "en": "and we now always end up on this team's t2 page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 389.2,
          "end": 391.47,
          "en": "if we tried to go anywhere else,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 391.47,
          "end": 394.2,
          "en": "but to another team-member that would also work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 394.2,
          "end": 397.62,
          "en": "But if I tried to go to users, I still end up on teams t2",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 397.62,
          "end": 400.053,
          "en": "because of this global before each hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 401.09000000000003,
          "end": 402.4,
          "en": "Now, I will say it again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 402.4,
          "end": 403.85,
          "en": "This of course is no logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 403.85,
          "end": 406.52,
          "en": "that really makes sense in this demo project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 406.52,
          "end": 409.03,
          "en": "but it is important that you understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 409.03,
          "end": 411.9,
          "en": "how this navigation guard works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 411.9,
          "end": 415.163,
          "en": "what the next method does in there and how you can use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 416.17,
          "end": 418.40999999999997,
          "en": "With that however, I'm going to comment this out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 418.40999999999997,
          "end": 421.87,
